<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matawai</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Matawai people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Matawai are a Maroon people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a>, descended from Africans who escaped from the plantations in the eighteenth century and settled along the Saramacca River. Closely related to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saramaka">Saramaka</a>, they made a peace treaty with the colonial government in 1767 that recognised their freedom in return for promises to return new runaways. They are among the smaller Maroon nations of the country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matawai.jpg" alt="Matawai" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julius Eduard Muller · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tropenmuseum_Royal_Tropical_Institute_Objectnumber_60008913_Granman_Adrai_Vroomhart_in_zijn_dorp.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
